=== PE 900: Cumulative Totients ===

Euler's totient φ(n) = #{k ≤ n : gcd(k,n) = 1}

=== Key identities ===
1. Σ_{d|n} φ(d) = n
2. φ(n) = n · Π_{p|n} (1 - 1/p)
3. Σ_{n=1}^{N} φ(n) ~ 3N²/π²  (asymptotic)

=== Computing Φ(N) efficiently ===
Using Dirichlet hyperbola method:
Φ(N) = N(N+1)/2 - Σ_{k=2}^{N} Φ(N/k)

This yields O(N^{2/3}) time via recursion + grouping.

=== Sublinear computation ===
We can compute Φ(N) for N up to ~10^11 in reasonable time
using the recursive formula with memoization.

=== Möbius-based formula ===
Φ(N) = 1/2 · Σ_{k=1}^{N} μ(k) · ⌊N/k⌋ · ⌊N/k+1⌋
Requires computing Mertens function M(N) = Σ μ(k).

